# Vulnerabilities reviewed and accepted for this image, not blanket-suppressed.
# Most entries below have no vendor-shipped fix available as of the scan
# date; the last two (msgpack, setuptools) do have fixes, but only in a
# dormant internal copy this image never executes (see their comment).
# None of these apply to how this container actually runs — no privileged
# mount operations, no systemd-homed, no SSH/TLS/proxy curl usage, no
# terminal UI, no ensurepip/venv calls at runtime.
# Re-run the scan periodically: if apt-get upgrade or a requirements.txt
# bump makes any of these actually reachable and fixed, drop the line
# instead of leaving it here as dead weight.

# util-linux (CVE-2026-76642, -78408, -78409, -78410): mount-helper /
# nsenter / X-mount privilege-escalation issues. This image never invokes
# mount, nsenter, or any util-linux mount tooling — it's a Python web
# service, not a container runtime or init system.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# libacl1 (CVE-2026-54369): symlink traversal via libacl's ACL handling.
# Nothing in this codebase manipulates POSIX ACLs or follows
# attacker-controlled symlinks through libacl.
CVE-2026-54369

# libsystemd0 (CVE-2026-16742): local privilege escalation via
# systemd-homed. systemd-homed does not run inside this container (no
# systemd as PID 1, no homed service).
CVE-2026-16742

# curl / libcurl4t64 (CVE-2026-12064, -8286, -8458, -8927): SSH host
# verification bypass on SFTP/SCP URLs, TLS config mismatch, connection
# reuse, and proxy-auth-state disclosure. The only curl invocation in this
# image is the Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK hitting plain HTTP on loopback
# (`curl -f http://localhost:8000/healthz`) — no SSH/SFTP/SCP, no TLS, no
# proxy, ever.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8458
CVE-2026-8927

# ncurses family — libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin
# (CVE-2025-69720): terminal buffer overflow. This is a headless FastAPI
# service; nothing here draws a terminal UI or links against ncurses.
CVE-2025-69720

# perl-base (CVE-2026-9538): Debian's own fix status is "fix_deferred" —
# they've decided not to backport it yet, not something apt-get upgrade
# can pull in. perl itself is never invoked by this application; it's
# part of the base OS layer only.
CVE-2026-9538

# msgpack (GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964) and setuptools CVE-2025-47273 at the old
# 70.3.0: both are Python's own ensurepip-bundled bootstrap wheel cache,
# not the site-packages copy pip actually resolves against — confirmed by
# the Dockerfile's `pip install --upgrade pip setuptools` installing a
# clean setuptools 84.0.0 into site-packages every build. This container
# never runs `python -m ensurepip` or `python -m venv`, so that bundled
# copy is dormant.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
